# Firmware include tree

Public firmware declarations live here. Exact operating values come from `config/` and `platformio.ini`; historical defaults in individual runtime structs are fallbacks, not the active deployment profile.

## Layout

- `app/`: node and base application coordinators.
- `calibration/`: command naming/status logging helpers.
- `config/`: authoritative network, sensing, power, base, and health constants.
- `drivers/`: small sensor-driver interfaces used for dependency injection.
- `interfaces/`: common clock, sensor, radio, analog, and TPS abstractions.
- `logging/`: structured `@SFDBG` logger and USB frame sink.
- `platform/`: Feather/SAMD21/RadioHead concrete adapters.
- `power/`: battery monitor and duty-cycle state machine.
- `radio/`: TDMA clock/config/service, TX queue, packet handler, TX-power controller.
- `sensors/`: sensor wrappers and trigger interface.
- `telemetry/`: `SensorSnapshot` and binary wire protocol.

## Current invariants

- `config/NetworkConfig.h` resolves shared `NUM_SLOTS=5` geometry from the build and defines 900 ms slots, two 20 ms guards, 150 ms receive wake-ahead, radio/reliability settings, and the 15-second active-build STATUS cadence.
- `telemetry/BinaryPacket.h` is the C++ wire-format authority. Keep it synchronized with `edge/edge-receiver/src/smartfires_edge/packet.py`.
- `interfaces/ISensor.h` supplies lifecycle and `fillSnapshot()`; sensors must not encode wire packets directly.
- `radio/TdmaConfig.h` contains safe member defaults, while `NetworkConfig::nodeTdmaProfile()` supplies values used by real node composition.
- Node assignment is runtime state derived from SAMD21 UID/`AWAKEN`; node ID is not a build-time slot constant.

Every `.h` and `.cpp` under `include/` and `src/` starts with the metadata format described by `documentation/CODE_FRONTMATTER.md`. Run `python3 documentation/check_code_headers.py` after changing current docs or firmware backlinks.
